{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold code generation pipeline task #5305 titled \"[stitch] cmd/md5sum -- srd030 R4.1-R4.3\". The task requires implementing three specific requirements from the md5sum SRD:\n   - R4.1: Must exit 0 when all files are processed and all verified digests match\n   - R4.2: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened, any digest fails verification, or the checksum file is unreadable\n   - R4.3: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n   \n   The files to modify are `cmd/md5sum/main.go` (add R4 functionality) and `cmd/md5sum/md5sum_test.go` (add differential tests for R4). Acceptance criteria require: compilation without errors, all tests passing, and all R4.1-R4.3 requirements implemented per the SRD.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: comparing Go binary output against GNU reference binary (gmd5sum from Homebrew)\n   - pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests for test execution\n   - pkg/hashutil for shared checksum logic (DigestFiles, VerifyChecksums, FormatGNU, FormatBSDTag, ParseChecksumLine, CheckOptions)\n   - pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler for SIGPIPE handling\n   - Exit code semantics: 0 for success, 1 for any failure\n   - GNU md5sum format: \"HASH  FILENAME\" (text) or \"HASH *FILENAME\" (binary)\n   - BSD tag format: \"MD5 (FILENAME) = HASH\"\n   - Cobbler stitch execution constitution with articles E1-E10\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd030-md5sum.yaml`\n     - Contains the full SRD specification for md5sum\n     - R4 section (lines 52-61) defines exit codes and SIGPIPE requirements:\n       ```yaml\n       R4:\n         title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n         items