xplicit test coverage\n\n   - `cmd/md5sum/md5sum_test.go` (248 lines)\n     - Uses differential testing pattern with gmd5sum reference binary\n     - Has 28 test cases covering R1, R2, R3 but no tests explicitly labeled for R4\n     - Some existing tests implicitly cover R4 behavior (ExitCode: 0 and ExitCode: 1 cases exist)\n     - Uses helper functions: `md5hex()` and `writeFile()`\n     - Creates temp files: hello.txt (\"hello\\n\"), empty.txt, and various checksum files (valid.md5, multi.md5, mismatch.md5, mixed.md5, malformed.md5, bsd.md5)\n     - Uses `discardStderr` normalizer to ignore stderr differences\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that R4.1-R4.3 are largely already implemented in the existing main.go code\n   - The primary remaining work is adding explicit R4-labeled differential test cases to md5sum_test.go\n   - Need to verify if any edge cases for R4.2 are missing (e.g., unreadable checksum file scenario)\n   - May need to add a test for SIGPIPE handling (R4.3), though this may be difficult to test differentially\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: The full stitch task prompt with role, repository_files, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement_states), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task description, shared_protocols, package_contracts, constraints, and description specifying the R4.1-R4.3 requirements for cmd/md5sum\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Modify `cmd/md5sum/main.go` if any R4 edge cases are missing (likely minimal changes since R4 functionality appears already implemented)\n   - Modify `cmd/md5sum/md5sum_test.go` to add explicit differential test cases for R4.1, R4.2, and R4.3\n   - Run `go build ./cmd/md5sum/` to v