{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wxmneh3Z94oEzGib2jtuHm","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have all the information needed. Let me provide you with a comprehensive report on these functions.\n\n## Summary of Key Functions\n\n### 1. `pkg/hashutil` - DigestFiles and VerifyChecksums\n\n#### **DigestFiles Function**\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5305/pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go` (lines 93-105)\n\n**Signature:**\n```go\nfunc DigestFiles(files []string, cfg HashConfig, binary, tag bool, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int\n```\n\n**Exit Codes:**\n- Returns `0` if all files are processed successfully\n- Returns `1` if any error occurs during file processing (file not found, unreadable file, etc.)\n\n**Error Handling:**\n- When a file cannot be opened or read, the error is printed to `stderr` in the format: `\"<filename>: <error_message>\"`\n- Processing continues for remaining files even if one fails\n- Uses `openInput()` helper which attempts to open the file; if it fails, the error is returned and printed\n- All file open errors (not found, permission denied, etc.) are wrapped and reported\n\n**Behavior:**\n- If `files` is empty or contains `\"-\"`, reads from stdin instead\n- For each file, computes the hash digest and prints it to `stdout`\n- Supports two output formats: BSD tag format (`--tag`) or GNU format (default)\n- In GNU format, the `binary` flag controls whether the output uses space or asterisk separator\n\n---\n\n#### **VerifyChecksums Function**\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5305/pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go` (lines 32-39)\n\n**Signature:**\n```go\nfunc VerifyChecksums(checksumFile string, cfg HashConfig, opts CheckOptions, stdout, stderr io.Writer) (bool, error)\n```\n\n**Return Values:**\n- First return: `bool` - `true` if all checksums verified successfully, `false` if any verification failed\n- Second return: `error` - returns error only if there's a problem opening or reading the checksum file itself\n\n**Error Handling:**\n- **File not found/unreadable:** Returns `error` with message like `\"opening checksum file: <underlying error>\"`\n- **Individual file errors during verification:** Handled in `verifyOneLine()` - prints `\"<filename>: FAILED open or read\"` to stdout but continues processing\n- **Malformed checksum lines:** If `--warn` flag is set (not `--status`), prints warning; still returns `true` for the line (doesn't fail overall verification)\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Reads the checksum file line-by-line\n- For each line, parses it (supports GNU and BSD tag formats)\n- Verifies each file's digest and reports results based on `CheckOptions`:\n  - `Status` flag: suppresses all output except exit status\n  - `Quiet` flag: suppresses OK messages\n  - `Warn` flag: enables warnings for malformed lines\n- Returns `false` (all checks didn't pass) if any file verification fails or any file cannot be opened/read\n\n---\n\n### 2. `pkg/sys` - InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5305/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (lines 17-24)\n\n**Signature:**\n```go\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n```\n\n**Purpose:**\nInstalls a signal handler for `SIGPIPE` that makes the process exit with code `0` when stdout or stderr is closed by a downstream consumer (matching GNU coreutils behavior).\n\n**Implementation Details:**\n- Creates a buffered channel with capacity 1\n- Uses `signal.Notify()` to listen for `SIGPIPE` signals (does NOT use `signal.Ignore`)\n- Spawns a goroutine that waits for the signal and calls `os.Exit(0)`\n- Safe to call multiple times; each call starts a new goroutine\n- Per the comments (R1.5, R1.6), this design avoids race conditions and allows multiple invocations"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"29dc1c8f-bac4-4231-acca-d13f8faa3c00","uuid